1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:02,540
Your cat sleeps up to sixteen hours a day,

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:03,970
and it's not being lazy.

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,930
Cats are ambush hunters.

4
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:07,810
They don't chase prey for miles.

5
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:11,800
They wait, then explode into a few seconds of full-speed sprinting,

6
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,650
and that burns a lot of energy.

7
00:00:13,830 --> 00:00:15,190
So they nap to save it.

8
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:16,720
They're not really night animals,

9
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:17,330
either.

10
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:19,320
They're built for dawn and dusk,

11
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:21,070
when mice are most active.

12
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:24,550
That's why your cat gets the zoomies right before sunrise.

13
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:26,920
Most of that sleep is light dozing,

14
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:27,450
too.

15
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:30,170
The ears keep turning toward every sound,

16
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:30,970
ready to go.

17
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,530
So if your cat is asleep on your bed right now,

18
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:34,400
don't wake it, because
